description: one stream in stream mode whose header, a setup and a parameters unit, comes in two packets
source: the draft of the toy format and its codec, spikes/input/README.md sections 2 and 3
target: toy
outcome: report
length: 57
# The setup is the whole payload of the first packet and the parameters of the second, so the codec gets the
# header in two deliveries, whatever the reads, and parses the second only with the continuation of the first:
# a continuation that is lost leaves the parameters without their setup, which is malformed.
---
## Toy format (spikes/input/README.md section 2): the file header
"CCToy" 00              # signature, "CCToy" and a zero byte
01                      # version 1
00                      # flags: none is defined
00 00 00 0c             # offset of the first element: 12, right after the header

## Toy format (section 2): the stream declaration, element STRM
"STRM"                  # code
00 00 00 07             # length of the body: 7
01                      # stream number 1
01                      # framing 1: stream mode
00                      # representation 0: units with one-byte lengths
"TCOD"                  # codec code: the toy codec

## Toy format (section 2): the first packet, element PACK
"PACK"                  # code
00 00 00 09             # length of the body: 9
01                      # stream number 1

## Toy codec (spikes/input/README.md section 3): the setup, kind 1, the first delivery
01                      # kind 1: setup
06                      # length 6
01 40                   # width 320
00 f0                   # height 240
01                      # parameter count 1
00                      # flags: none, so the parameters can be read

## Toy format (section 2): the second packet, element PACK
"PACK"                  # code
00 00 00 05             # length of the body: 5
01                      # stream number 1

## Toy codec (section 3): the parameters, kind 2, the second delivery
02                      # kind 2: parameters
02                      # length 2: the setup's one 16-bit parameter
00 07                   # parameter 7
